IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fja-courts`

-- Family Justice Act 2014, ss 10, 11A to 11C, 23, 26(3A), 33, 34 and the Second Schedule -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_fja.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a barred variation application filed without permission` MEANS Filing WITH
    `a filing restriction order is in force` IS TRUE
    `permission was obtained` IS FALSE
    `is itself an application for permission` IS FALSE

`the same with permission` MEANS Filing WITH
    `a filing restriction order is in force` IS TRUE
    `permission was obtained` IS TRUE
    `is itself an application for permission` IS FALSE

`an application for permission to file` MEANS Filing WITH
    `a filing restriction order is in force` IS TRUE
    `permission was obtained` IS FALSE
    `is itself an application for permission` IS TRUE

`an ordinary application` MEANS Filing WITH
    `a filing restriction order is in force` IS FALSE
    `permission was obtained` IS FALSE
    `is itself an application for permission` IS FALSE

§ `s 10`

#ASSERT `the hearing is in private` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the hearing is in private` TRUE

#ASSERT `the publisher commits the section 10 offence` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the publisher commits the section 10 offence` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the publisher commits the section 10 offence` TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment in months for breaching a publication order` EQUALS 36

§ `s 11A`

#ASSERT `the filing is treated as dismissed automatically` `a barred variation application filed without permission`
#ASSERT NOT `the filing is treated as dismissed automatically` `the same with permission`
#ASSERT NOT `the filing is treated as dismissed automatically` `an application for permission to file`
#ASSERT NOT `the filing is treated as dismissed automatically` `an ordinary application`

#ASSERT `the ground supports a filing restriction` `likely without merit given past conduct`
#ASSERT `the ground supports a filing restriction` `likely to harm the child's welfare`
#ASSERT `the ground supports a filing restriction` `likely to impede resolution of pending proceedings`
#ASSERT NOT `the ground supports a filing restriction` `inconvenient to the other party`

§ `s 11B`

#ASSERT `the court may make the order of its own motion` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make the order of its own motion` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the court may make the order of its own motion` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 26(3A)`

#ASSERT `the court to apply to first` TRUE EQUALS "a Family Court"
#ASSERT `the court to apply to first` FALSE EQUALS "the court with jurisdiction"

§ `s 23`

#ASSERT NOT `permission is needed to appeal from the Family Court` `a maintenance order`
#ASSERT NOT `permission is needed to appeal from the Family Court` `a custody order`
#ASSERT NOT `permission is needed to appeal from the Family Court` `a division of matrimonial assets`
#ASSERT `permission is needed to appeal from the Family Court` `unconditional permission to defend`
#ASSERT `permission is needed to appeal from the Family Court` `an unconditional setting aside of a default judgment`
#ASSERT `permission is needed to appeal from the Family Court` `a Protection from Harassment Act protection order`

#ASSERT NOT `an ordinary money judgment needs permission to appeal` `a Family Court` 10000
#ASSERT `an ordinary money judgment needs permission to appeal` `a District Court in a civil case` 10000
#ASSERT NOT `an ordinary money judgment needs permission to appeal` `a District Court in a civil case` 100000

§ `ss 33, 34`

#ASSERT `an appeal can be brought despite the agreement` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `an appeal can be brought despite the agreement` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `an appeal can be brought despite the agreement` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `the order may be enforced pending appeal` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the order may be enforced pending appeal` TRUE

